        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the case in hand, the complaint and the conviction is also relatable to an allegation which says that the material/food seized from the possession of the accused petitioners were adulterated."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b9366a4bf70c4e6eb11eaef7185d6ff3_33",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, learned counsel, in the considered opinion of this Court, is correct in arguing that such conviction is relatable to Section 51 of the Act, 2006."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "92d0a2ac66f646b0a0b4bb764f3c1faa_34",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "13. Therefore, in the given context of the present case, this Court is of the view that the determination made in Trilok Chand (supra) and M/s A.K.Sarkar (supra) can be made applicable to the facts of the present case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3a5b2032f2794d0e85a47dae590b5598_35",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
